                    <history>
                        <origin><origDate calendar="#Hijri-qamari" when="1623" cert="high">1033 AH
                                (1623 CE)</origDate></origin>
                        <provenance><p>Previously in the collection of <persName type="supplied"
                            key="person_f830" role="fmo">Colonel George William Hamilton
                            (1807-1868)</persName> who served in <placeName
                                ref="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/tgn/7000208">India</placeName>
                            <date calendar="#Gregorian" from="1823" to="1867"> from 1823 to
                                1867</date>, latterly as Commissioner of <placeName
                                    ref="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/tgn/7001535">Delhi</placeName>. He
                            acquired over a thousand Indian and Persian manuscripts, from which the
                            <orgName type="standard" key="person_134857252">British
                                Museum</orgName> selected 352, now held in the <orgName
                                    type="standard" key="person_121814978">British Library</orgName>;
                            his ownership inscription on <locus from="flyleaf_ia">flyleaf
                                ia</locus>:  description of the contents by Hamilton's assistant. Hamilton's label on
                            <locus from="Back_paste-down">back paste-down</locus>:
                            <quote>Hamilton MSS 33</quote></p></provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>
                                <name source="#viaf" key="97751058" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">Alexander Lindsay, 25th Earl of Crawford (1812-1880), book collector and writer on art</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Crawford, Alexander Crawford Lindsay, 1812-1880</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <name source="#viaf" key="9985420" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">James Ludovic Lindsay, 26th Earl of Crawford (1847-1913), astronomer and book collector</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Crawford, James Ludovic Lindsay, Earl of, 1847-1913</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>Formerly in the Crawford Library (Bibliotheca Lindesiana) at Haigh Hall, Lancashire, which was formed and developed by Alexander and James Ludovic Lindsay.</p>
                            <p>His bookplate on <locus from="Back_paste-down">back paste-down</locus>: <quote>Bibliotheca Lindesiana 3/C</quote>.</p>                        </provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>
                                <name role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">Enriqueta Rylands (1843-1908), philanthropist and founder of The John Rylands Library</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Rylands, Enriqueta, 1843-1908</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>Purchased by Enriqueta Rylands in <date when="1901">1901</date> from James Ludovic Lindsay, 26th Earl of Crawford (1847-1913).</p>
                        </provenance>
                        <acquisition>
                            <p>Bequeathed by <name role="dnr">
